{
"classname" "game_messagebox"
"origin" "-376 -296 200"
"targetname" "info_screen"
"title" "A world screen"
"message" "The screen is a vgui_screen with Panel Name example_screen (ui/scripts/screens/example_screen.res, which the game comes with), Width 128 and Height 64, and a yaw of 270 so it faces south. Its origin is the screen's lower-left corner as seen from the front.\n\nThe layout has two buttons with the commands hello and light. The screen reacts to them with the keys ~hello (hello_mm) and ~light (lamp), which you add with SmartEdit off.\n\nhello_mm shows a game_text and fires a vgui_control_proxy, which writes a new line into the layout's Status label. lamp is a light and an env_sprite with the same name."
}
